        "comments": "The assembly lpCarBige1.hap2.1 is based on 52x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using PacBio and Hi-C data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. The two haplotypes do not show simple one-to-one chromosome synteny, with some homologous regions occurring on different chromosomes between haplotypes. Elevated read coverage across chromosome 13 (9,953?12,529 Kbp) suggests that additional copies of this sequence may exist in the genome and that this region is therefore underrepresented in the assembly.",
